\par 
\par ## Root-cause families
\par 
\par - **F1 \emdash  Sentinel-0 encoding reused by the violation checker** (Bugs 1\endash 3). The
\par   encoder fills "unknown" fields with `0`, a value designed only for GA scoring;
\par   `violations.py` treats those zeros as real category/number values.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid3361506 - **F2 \emdash  Spec \u8596\'3f code drift** (Bug 4).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\insrsid3361506\charrsid3361506 - **F3 \emdash  Re-match concurrency & lifecycle** (Bugs 5\endash 9).
\par - **F4 \emdash  Missing input validation / robustness** (Bugs 10\endash 12).
\par 
\par ---
\par 
\par ## F1 \emdash  Encoder sentinel leaks into violations
\par 
\par ### Bug 1 \emdash  Form-less student masks diversity violations *(High)*
\par **Where:** `violations.py` (gender/job/education/experience rules) + `encoder.py`
\par `prepare_data` form-less branch.
\par **What:** A roster student with no `StudentProfile` is encoded with every categorical
\par feature at `0` (gender\u8594\'3fmale, job\u8594\'3fnone, \'85). In a team, that fabricated value looks like
\par a distinct category and **suppresses a real homogeneity warning**.
\par **Repro:** Team of two real students both `gender=female` + one form-less student;
\par gender weight > 0 \u8594\'3f no `gender` warning, although the only known data is all-female.
\par **Fix:** Represent "unknown" distinctly (e.g. mask form-less rows out of the
\par diversity/std computations), or require a profile before matching.
\par **Test:** `tests_bugs_extra.py::FormlessProfileCorruptsViolationsBugTests`.
\par 
\par ### Bug 2 \emdash  Form-less student fabricates age spread *(High)*
\par **Where:** same as Bug 1; `age` rule, `encoder.py:107`.
\par **What:** Form-less age \u8594\'3f `0`. Mixed with a real age (e.g. 21) this manufactures a
\par large std and **suppresses the "no age spread" warning**.
\par **Repro:** one real student age 21 + one form-less; age weight > 0 \u8594\'3f no `age` warning.
\par **Fix:** as Bug 1.
\par **Test:** `tests_bugs_extra.py::FormlessProfileCorruptsViolationsBugTests`.
\par 
\par ### Bug 3 \emdash  Blank age on a real profile \u8594\'3f encoded 0 *(Med)*
\par **Where:** `encoder.py:107` (`if student.age is not None`), consumed by `violations.py:144`.
\par **What:** `age` is nullable. A student who filled the form but left age blank is
\par encoded as age `0` \emdash  same corruption as Bug 2, but for **active, real users**.
\par **Repro:** two real profiles, ages 21 and `None`; age weight > 0 \u8594\'3f no `age` warning.
\par **Fix:** skip `None` ages from the std (compute over known ages only); flag if < 2 known.
\par **Test:** `tests_bugs_extra.py::BlankAgeSentinelBugTests`.
\par 
\par ## F2 \emdash  Spec \u8596\'3f code drift
\par 
\par ### Bug 4 \emdash  `tasks` not evaluated for size-1 teams *(Low)*
\par **Where:** `violations.py:161` (`count >= 2` gate) vs Appendix C.2 of `req/task6.md`.
\par **What:** C.2 lists `tasks` among the rules that apply to size-1 teams; the code gates
\par it behind `count >= 2`, so a lone member with no task preference is never flagged.
\par **Fix (pick one):** drop `tasks` from C.2's size-1 sentence, **or** lower the gate to
\par `count >= 1`. See `C2_RECONCILIATION.md`.
\par **Test:** `tests_bugs_extra.py::TasksSizeOneDocDriftBugTests`.
\par 
\par ## F3 \emdash  Re-match concurrency & lifecycle
\par 
\par ### Bug 5 \emdash  Student locked *during* a running re-match is still moved *(High)*
\par **Where:** `views.py:231` (`_run_rematch` commit loop).
\par **What:** `_run_rematch` snapshots the unlocked members before the GA. At commit it
\par re-checks **team** locks (`currently_locked_team_ids`) but **not** whether an
\par individual student was locked while the GA ran. A student the teacher locks mid-run is
\par therefore still reassigned \emdash  directly contradicting the lock contract.
\par **Repro:** start a re-match on a large roster; lock a single student while the progress
\par bar is moving; on completion that student has been moved.
\par **Fix:** in the commit loop, re-query `is_locked` per membership (or re-filter
\par `TeamMembership` for `is_locked=False` inside the transaction) and skip locked ones.
\par **Verify:** SERVER_TEST_PLAN R-8 variant (lock a *student*, not a team, mid-run).
\par 
\par ### Bug 6 \emdash  `rematch_cancel_requested` is dead state; cross-process cancel fails *(High in multi-worker; N/A single-worker)*
\par **Where:** flag set at `views.py:830`; reset in `_claim_rematch_token` /
\par `_release_rematch_token`; **read nowhere**. Cancellation actually works via the
\par in-process `cancel_event` found through `_PROGRESS_QUEUES`.
\par **What:** The model docstring says "the GA checks this [DB] flag after each generation".
\par It does not \emdash  nothing reads `rematch_cancel_requested`. Cancellation depends on an
\par in-memory dict, so a cancel request handled by a **different worker process** than the
\par one running the GA finds no queue entry and silently does nothing. (The README's
\par "use 1 worker, many threads" rule is effectively a workaround for this.)
\par **Fix:** have `_wrapped_on_generation` also re-read `rematch_cancel_requested` from the
\par DB (e.g. every N generations) so cancellation works across processes; or document the
\par single-worker constraint as load-bearing.
\par **Verify:** SERVER_TEST_PLAN R-3 under a 2-worker gunicorn \u8594\'3f cancel from a second tab.
\par 
\par ### Bug 7 \emdash  `connection.close()` precedes further DB writes in the worker `finally` *(Med, PostgreSQL)*
\par **Where:** `views.py:714`, before `mark_completed`, `_release_rematch_token`,
\par `_release_db_lock`.
\par **What:** Closing the connection auto-releases any PostgreSQL **advisory lock** held by
\par that session \emdash  *before* the token row is cleared. The subsequent ORM calls then
\par silently reopen a new connection, and `_release_db_lock` runs `pg_advisory_unlock` on a
\par connection that never held the lock (no-op). Harmless on SQLite; on PostgreSQL it
\par creates a brief window where the advisory lock is released but the token still set, and
\par the explicit unlock does nothing.
\par **Fix:** move `connection.close()` to the very end of `finally`, after token/lock
\par release and the audit write.
\par **Verify:** code review + PostgreSQL integration test.
\par 
\par ### Bug 8 \emdash  Small unlocked set crashes the GA via re-match *(Med)*
\par **Where:** `_run_rematch` \u8594\'3f `genetic_matcher.match()` team-count arithmetic (`n_teams`
\par floors to 0 when `unlocked < min_size`).
\par **What:** The documented small-roster generation bug is reachable through a **new
\par path**: lock most students so only 1\endash 2 remain unlocked with `min_size=3` \u8594\'3f the GA gets
\par `n_teams=0` \u8594\'3f empty `gene_space` \u8594\'3f crash. The run ends as `error` in the audit log.
\par **Fix:** guard `_run_rematch` (and/or `match`) when `unlocked < min_size`: skip with a
\par `noop`/clear message instead of running the GA.
\par **Verify:** SERVER_TEST_PLAN \emdash  lock all but one student, then Re-match.
\par 
\par ### Bug 9 \emdash  SSE `finally` cancels in-flight work on any disconnect *(Med)*
\par **Where:** `views.py:796` (`event_stream` `finally: cancel_event.set()`).
\par **What:** The `finally` fires on **every** stream exit, so a transient proxy/network
\par disconnect (not a user cancel) sets `cancel_event`, the worker discards its result, and
\par the suppressed auto-reconnect means the run is silently lost. Intended for deliberate
\par disconnects, but indistinguishable from accidental ones.
\par **Fix:** only cancel on disconnect if the worker has not already signalled "done"
\par (track completion), or require an explicit cancel call rather than inferring it from
\par stream teardown.
\par **Verify:** SERVER_TEST_PLAN R-5 (kill the stream mid-run) vs a normal completion.
\par 
\par ## F4 \emdash  Input validation / robustness
\par 
\par ### Bug 10 \emdash  `api_move_student` 500s on a non-numeric `team_id` *(Med)*
\par **Where:** `views.py:472` \emdash  `get_object_or_404(Team, pk=int(team_id), \'85)`.
\par **What:** `membership_id` is validated inside the `try`, but `team_id` is not; the later
\par `int(team_id)` is outside the guard. A body like `\{"membership_id": 1, "team_id":"abc"\}`
\par raises an uncaught `ValueError` \u8594\'3f **HTTP 500** instead of a clean `400 invalid_input`.
\par **Fix:** validate/parse `team_id` inside the same `try` (e.g.
\par `team_id = int(team_id) if team_id is not None else None`).
\par **Test:** `tests_bugs_extra.py::MoveTeamIdValidationBugTests` (added).
\par 
\par ### Bug 11 \emdash  Duplicate usernames in the CSV crash generation *(Med)*
\par **Where:** `views.py:327` (`bulk_create`) vs `TeamMembership` `unique_together
\par (session, username)`.
\par **What:** A roster with a repeated `username` violates the constraint \u8594\'3f
\par `IntegrityError` \u8594\'3f HTTP 500 with no actionable message.
\par **Fix:** de-duplicate or validate usernames before persisting and surface a form error
\par naming the duplicates.
\par **Verify:** upload a CSV with one repeated username (SERVER_TEST_PLAN G-3 variant).
\par 
\par ### Bug 12 \emdash  Malformed / username-less CSV 500s instead of a form error *(Med)*
\par **Where:** `views.py:259` (`pd.read_csv`) and `views.py` `row["username"]`.
\par **What:** The form checks that a file was supplied, not that it parses as CSV or
\par contains a `username` column. A malformed file or a missing column raises inside the
\par view \u8594\'3f HTTP 500.
\par **Fix:** wrap parsing in `try/except`, validate required columns, and re-render the form
\par with a clear error.
\par **Verify:** SERVER_TEST_PLAN G-3.
\par 
