\par ## What I checked and found **clean** (refuted hypotheses \emdash  for transparency)
\par 
\par - **Row-order in `prepare_data`:** preserves CSV order (`iterrows` + append), so the
\par   `encoded[i] \u8596\'3f memberships[i]` assumption in `violations.py` is sound. Not a bug.
\par - **Re-match new-team naming:** `existing_names` is re-queried per iteration and the
\par   `while` loop skips taken names, so no `unique_together` collision. Not a bug.
\par - **`col_idx` offsets:** consistent with `encode_student`'s column layout. Not a bug.
\par - **`mark_completed` field allow-list:** correctly rejects typo'd kwargs. Works as
\par   intended.
\par - **Template label/icon drift:** labels/icons are injected from the backend via
\par   `json_script`, not hard-coded in JS. No drift.
\par 
